.TH LYRICVID 1 "August 2026" "LyricVid 0.8.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lyricvid \- create Whisper-aligned Remotion lyric videos and upload them to YouTube
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lyricvid
.RI [ folder ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B lyricvid styles
.br
.B lyricvid jobs
.br
.B lyricvid upload
.I video
.B --title
.I title
.RI [ upload-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
LyricVid is a command-line video composition pipeline for music, lyric videos, narrated visualizers, technical explainers, and social-media variants. It combines authored lyric metadata, ffprobe, Mutagen, faster-whisper, sequence alignment, Remotion, FFmpeg, optional artwork and voice-over, detached background jobs, and OAuth-based YouTube publishing.
.PP
Authored lyrics are treated as the displayed source of truth whenever available. Whisper is used primarily as an acoustic timing layer. This allows the rendered video to preserve exact spelling, punctuation, capitalization, and authored section structure while using the performed audio to determine timing.
.PP
By default LyricVid scans the current directory and writes results to a lyric-videos directory beneath the input folder.
.SH LYRIC SOURCE ORDER
With
.B --lyrics-source auto
LyricVid prefers exact authored lyrics before falling back to Whisper-only transcription:
.PP
1. lyric metadata discovered by ffprobe / embedded media tags
.br
2. embedded metadata read by Mutagen
.br
3. matching sidecar lyric files
.br
4. Whisper transcription when authored lyrics are unavailable
.PP
Whisper timing anchors are sequence-aligned to authored tokens. Unmatched authored tokens may be interpolated between reliable anchors. Conservative non-overlapping display windows are used to reduce brief lyric flashes between actual sung lines.
.SH INPUTS
Supported audio includes MP3, WAV, M4A, FLAC, AAC, OGG, and OPUS. Artwork may be PNG, JPG/JPEG, or WebP. Motion backgrounds may be MP4, MOV, WebM, or MKV.
.SH PRIMARY OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --model " MODEL"
Select the faster-whisper model. Default: small.en. Larger models can improve recognition at the cost of memory and render preparation time.
.TP
.BI --language " CODE"
Language code or auto. Default: en.
.TP
.BI --lyrics-source " auto|ffprobe|embedded|sidecar|whisper"
Select lyric text source policy.
.TP
.BI --image " FILE"
Use artwork in the composition.
.TP
.BI --artist " NAME"
Artist displayed in the composition. If omitted, LyricVid may use embedded artist metadata.
.TP
.BI --brand " TEXT"
Top-left brand label. Default: Richmack Radio.
.TP
.BI --intro-seconds " N"
Prepend an artwork intro for N seconds. Audio and lyric timing are delayed so the song remains synchronized after the intro.
.TP
.BI --outro-seconds " N"
Append an outro after the song.
.TP
.BI --outro-image " FILE"
Artwork for the outro. Defaults to the main --image when omitted.
.TP
.BI --outro-text " TEXT"
Outro text. Default: Thanks for listening.
.TP
.BI --image-mode " background|card|logo"
Select artwork presentation mode.
.TP
.BI --background-video " FILE"
Use an explicit looping motion background.
.TP
.BI --voiceover " FILE"
Layer narration or another voice track over the music.
.TP
.BI --music-volume " 0.0-1.0"
Music gain multiplier. Default: 1.0.
.TP
.BI --voiceover-volume " 0.0-1.0"
Voice-over gain multiplier. Default: 1.0.
.TP
.BI --layout " cyber|minimal|terminal"
Base Remotion layout.
.TP
.BI --style " NAME"
Apply a preset that controls layout, theme, and artwork treatment. Use lyricvid styles to list available presets.
.TP
.BI --format " landscape|short|square"
Output canvas. landscape=1280x720, short=1080x1920, square=1080x1080.
.TP
.BI --device " cpu|cuda|auto"
Inference device.
.TP
.BI --compute-type " TYPE"
Whisper compute type. Default: int8. float16 is commonly used with CUDA.
.TP
.BI --threads " N"
Worker threads used for CPU work.
.TP
.BI --jobs " N"
Parallel job count for batch operation.
.TP
.BI --crf " N"
H.264 constant-rate-factor quality value. Lower values increase quality and file size. Default: 24.
.TP
.BI -o " DIR", " --output " DIR
Set output directory.
.TP
.B --recursive
Search recursively for supported audio.
.TP
.B --force
Overwrite existing rendered MP4 files without necessarily discarding cached Whisper alignment.
.TP
.B --retranscribe
Ignore cached transcript/alignment data and run Whisper again.
.TP
.B --transcribe-only
Perform lyric extraction and timing alignment without rendering the final video.
.TP
.B --studio
Prepare the project and open Remotion Studio for interactive preview.
.TP
.B --lyrics-info
Show discovered lyric sources without running Whisper.
.TP
.B --doctor
Check required external dependencies and runtime paths.
.TP
.B --clean-cache
Remove LyricVid runtime and transcript caches.
.TP
.B --detach, --background-job
Relaunch the current operation in a detached process. Output is written under ~/.cache/lyricvid/jobs and survives terminal closure or SSH disconnect.
.TP
.B --version
Print version.
.SH STYLE PRESETS
Current presets include cyberpunk, terminal-green, daemon-red, root-violet, system-amber, network-teal, neon-pink, minimal-clean, podcast, explainer, and metro-cinematic.
.PP
.B metro-cinematic
uses a restrained music-video treatment with album art, soft metro motion, film-grain styling, reduced HUD clutter, and neon accents.
.SH SECTION LABELS
Authored lines that represent structural labels such as [Verse 1], [Chorus], [Bridge], and [Outro] are rendered as section labels rather than sung lyric lines. Their timing is kept separate from karaoke word highlighting.
.SH DETACHED JOBS
Run a long render in the background:
.PP
.nf
lyricvid . --style metro-cinematic --detach
.fi
.PP
List recent jobs:
.PP
.nf
lyricvid jobs
.fi
.PP
Each detached job has metadata and a log under ~/.cache/lyricvid/jobs. The start message prints the exact tail -f command for following progress.
.SH YOUTUBE UPLOAD
The upload command publishes an existing video with YouTube Data API v3 and OAuth 2.0.
.PP
.nf
lyricvid upload video.mp4 \\
  --title "Artist - Song | Official Lyric Video" \\
  --description-file description.md \\
  --tags "artist,song,lyric video" \\
  --public
.fi
.PP
Uploads are private by default. Use --public or --unlisted to change visibility.
.SH YOUTUBE OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --title " TEXT"
Required title. YouTube maximum: 100 characters.
.TP
.BI --description " TEXT"
Inline description. Mutually exclusive with --description-file.
.TP
.BI --description-file " FILE"
Read UTF-8 description text or Markdown from a file. Use - to read stdin. If neither description option is supplied, LyricVid also checks video.description.txt, video.description.md, and video.youtube.txt sidecars.
.TP
.BI --tags " CSV"
Comma-separated tags.
.TP
.BI --category " ID"
YouTube category ID. Default: 22.
.TP
.B --public
Publish publicly.
.TP
.B --unlisted
Publish as unlisted.
.TP
.BI --credentials " FILE"
OAuth desktop-client JSON. Default: .secrets/youtube-oauth.json relative to the current working directory.
.TP
.BI --token " FILE"
Cached OAuth token. Default: .secrets/youtube-token.json.
.TP
.BI --chunk-mb " N"
Resumable upload chunk size in MiB. Default: 8.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Validate and print upload metadata without authenticating or uploading.
.TP
.B --detach
Perform an already-authenticated upload as a detached background job.
.SH OAUTH SECURITY
Never commit OAuth client-secret JSON or token files. Keep .secrets ignored by Git and restrict local credential permissions where possible.
.SH YOUTUBE QUALITY NOTE
A newly uploaded HD video can initially appear at 360p while YouTube finishes higher-resolution transcodes. LyricVid uploads the source MP4; final playback resolutions are generated asynchronously by YouTube.
.SH EXAMPLES
Render the current folder with a cyberpunk preset:
.PP
.nf
lyricvid . --style cyberpunk
.fi
.PP
Metro-cinematic single with intro and outro:
.PP
.nf
lyricvid . \\
  --style metro-cinematic \\
  --image cover.png \\
  --artist "Esoterica" \\
  --brand "Richmack Radio" \\
  --intro-seconds 5 \\
  --outro-seconds 7 \\
  --outro-text "COMPETE FOR YOU - ESOTERICA" \\
  --detach
.fi
.PP
Narrated explainer with reduced music volume:
.PP
.nf
lyricvid . \\
  --style explainer \\
  --voiceover narration.mp3 \\
  --music-volume 0.25 \\
  --voiceover-volume 1.0
.fi
.PP
Vertical social version:
.PP
.nf
lyricvid . --style neon-pink --format short
.fi
.PP
Inspect authored lyrics only:
.PP
.nf
lyricvid . --lyrics-info
.fi
.PP
Force fresh acoustic alignment:
.PP
.nf
lyricvid . --retranscribe --force
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/lyricvid/
Shared runtime and transcript cache.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/lyricvid/jobs/
Detached-job logs and metadata.
.TP
.I lyric-videos/alignment-report.json
Per-track lyric-alignment QA report.
.TP
.I .secrets/youtube-oauth.json
Default YouTube OAuth client file.
.TP
.I .secrets/youtube-token.json
Default cached YouTube OAuth token.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Use lyricvid --doctor to verify Node, npm, ffprobe, Python, cache paths, and runtime paths. For detached jobs use lyricvid jobs and tail the printed log file.
.PP
If first-run Whisper output appears idle while CPU usage is high, model download or acoustic inference may still be active. Hugging Face can warn about unauthenticated requests when no HF_TOKEN is configured.
.SH DOCUMENTATION AS CODE
The repository contains docs/architecture.d2. Render it with scripts/render-docs.sh after installing D2. README screenshots can be generated from a completed MP4 with scripts/capture-readme-frames.mjs and Playwright.
